# x86 Backend Post-Fixes Summary — Consolidated Audit

Logline: Per-fix table, hostile-probe-v2 attribution, and remaining risks for the nine fixes that landed across the x86 backend after the 6,936-fixture hostile probe v2.

Setup: Reads seven audit files (x86-hostile-probe-v2, x86-ssa-post-fix-projection, x86-5shape-refuse-post-fix, x86-runtime-blob-tail, x86-ast-typed-shim, simd-deep, x86_emit_final/x86_emit_post_fix). No .oo file was modified. No compiler was run. The nine fixes are: silent fall-through, 5-shape refuse gate, per-arm wrote counter, SSA per-block remap, SSA Float gaps, SIMD Float fix, dead-arm deletes, dead-import removal, contract-gate expansion. References use file:line where the evidence lives.

Beats:
  1. Build the per-fix table across all nine fixes.
  2. Attribute each hostile-probe-v2 failure to the fix that catches it.
  3. List the remaining risks in priority order.
  4. State the consolidated final state.

