## 1. Per-fix table

Nine fixes landed. Pre-fix state is the hostile-probe-v2 baseline or the pre-fix static reading; post-fix state is the static reading after the fix landed. Sources cite the audit that documents the fix and the residual risk.

| # | Fix | Pre-fix state | Post-fix state | Source | Remaining risk |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Silent fall-through | Typed-AST shim `Err(_) => { }` arm swallowed errors and fell through to the 22-arm chain, producing wrong assembly. | `x86_emit.oo:90` now does `Err(typed_e) => { println(typed_e); process_exit(1); }`. | x86_emit_post_fix.oot §2 row 3; x86_emit_final.oot row 4. | The 22-arm chain is still reachable from a non-typed source. Turn 2 (line 94 TODO) will collapse the chain; until then the shim can be bypassed by code that fails the typed shim's pre-checks but passes the chain. |
| 2 | 5-shape refuse gate | Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T] reached the 22-arm chain and produced no-op main or hardcoded bodies. | `x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo` (238 lines) refuses the 5 shapes at dispatch via `x86_emit_shape_refuse_test` at `x86_emit.oo:73-84`. 5/5 Sig + RealH + Msg pass. | x86-5shape-refuse-post-fix.oot §1-§2. | 3 over/under-refusal smells: Shape 1 real-handler only accepts `println(ident)` not `println(a+b)`, Shape 4 misses bare `struct S { ... }`, Shape 5 misses `list_get`/`list_set`. 5/5 ERR messages are clear. |
| 3 | Per-arm wrote counter | 7 dedicated arms (struct, list, opt, free, typed_let, match, fib, heap) emitted `push %rbp; sub $64, %rsp; add $64, %rsp; pop %rbp; syscall` with zero writes. 2,595 of 2,607 empty-stdout binaries. | `wrote` flag set on every write syscall; `if !wrote { process_exit(1) }` after the body loop. Per-arm convert. | x86-runtime-blob-tail.oot §6.1; x86-post-fix-projection.oot §2. | Arms not on the counter list (while, for, channel, parallel) still produce no-op main. Estimated 221 more empty-stdout sources. Counter must be added per arm. |
| 4 | SSA per-block remap | 92.6% ASM-FAIL on SSA: 3,215 duplicate `.Lxss_pi_*` labels + 3,211 undefined `.Lmain_block*` forward refs. | `x86_ssa_emit.oo:101` suffixes labels with `inst_id.to_string()` for uniqueness. `x86_ssa_emit_function` line 44 emits one label per block. | x86-ssa-post-fix-projection.oot §2.1-§2.2; x86-post-fix-projection.oot §3. | V1 14-fixture `movq` operand-widening bug may or may not be fixed. Block-name collision within a function is not statically guarded. Central estimate: 0.0% ASM-FAIL; upper bound 2.1% if v1 bug not fixed. |
| 5 | SSA Float gaps | `parse_v` at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:25-37` had no `e/E` exponent branch. `op_v` at line 58 returned 0 silently on `b == 0`. | Sci-notation branch copied from `x86_float_parse:46-61`. SSA divide-by-zero now fail-closed like the non-SSA path. | simd-deep.oot gaps #2, #3. | SSA Float path is still un-tested by the smoke (`x86_ssa_float_runtime_smoke.oo:56-98` only checks SSE asm). New sci-notation path inherits non-SSA overflow characteristics. |
| 6 | SIMD Float fix | `x86_float_fold_atom` at `x86_emit_float.oo:117-134` lost the sign on `-0.0` literals. `x86_collect_and_emit_float:200-218` only set `neg_zero` on chain MINUS, not on atom sign. | Atom sign propagates into `neg_zero`. `-0.0` literal now emits `.double -0.0`. | simd-deep.oot gap #1, fix order #1. | 9 of 10 gaps remain: 32-bit `cvttsd2si` truncation for `|value| > 2^31`, no NaN/Inf detection, stack overrun for very large integers, i64 STAR overflow, sci-notation positive-exp overflow. |
| 7 | Dead-arm DELETEs | Some arms in the 22-arm chain (e.g. while, for, fib, heap) had loose matchers and empty-body emitters. | 2 dead imports removed (`x86_emit_list.oo`, `x86_emit_diag.oo`); 31 → 29 imports; 211 → 209 lines. | x86_emit_post_fix.oot §3; x86_emit_final.oot row 9. | Arms themselves were NOT deleted. The chain still has 22 arms; several still have the no-op main failure mode. The fix only removed the import surface, not the arm bodies. |
| 8 | Dead imports removed | `x86_emit_list.oo` (5 pub fn, 0 callers) and `x86_emit_diag.oo` (7 pub fn, 0 callers) imported but never referenced from `x86_emit.oo`. | Both imports removed at `x86_emit.oo:16-44`. List runtime now lives only in the runtime registry; diag helpers are imported only by call sites that need them. | x86_emit_post_fix.oot §3; x86_emit_final.oot row 9. | List runtime is unreachable from the dispatcher (intentional, the 5-shape gate kills `List[T]`). Diag helpers are imported by other files (smokes, c-emit). No remaining dead-import smell in `x86_emit.oo`. |
| 9 | Contract gate expanded | Contract gate at `x86_emit.oo:48-57` ran with 4 clauses (`x86_emit_contract.oo:160,175`); some float-typed and struct-shaped sources passed. | New clauses added: covers 4 conditions; rejects float-typed, struct-shaped, and several ad-hoc violations. Wired at the top of `x86_emit_stream` before secret + shape gates. | x86_emit_final.oot row 11-12; x86-smoke-coverage.oot row 05. | Contract gate and empty-source check overlap by design (defense-in-depth, `x86_emit_final.oot` Issue 4). 3 of 42 modules have no direct smoke; contract-gate coverage matrix is not exhaustive. |

Row count: 9 (one per fix). Acceptance criterion: ≥7.

