## 4. Final state summary

| Metric | Pre-fix (v2) | Post-fix (central estimate) | Δ |
|---|---|---|---|
| emit-x86 COMPILED | 5,750 / 6,936 (82.9%) | ~3,143 / 6,936 (45.3%) | -2,607 (now REFUSED) |
| emit-x86 REFUSED | 1,185 / 6,936 (17.1%) | ~3,792 / 6,936 (54.7%) | +2,607 |
| Silent-miscompile rate (% of COMPILED) | 45.3% (2,607 / 5,750) | ~0.4% (12 / 3,143) | -44.9 pp |
| emit-x86-ssa COMPILED | 508 / 6,936 (7.3%) | ~6,928 / 6,936 (99.9%) | +6,420 |
| emit-x86-ssa ASM-FAIL | 6,426 / 6,936 (92.6%) | ~7 / 6,936 (0.1%) | -92.5 pp |
| Real-write-wrong-string | ~12 | ~12 | 0 (Turn 2 work) |

**Status: PARTIAL.** The 9 fixes converted the dominant silent-miscompile class (no-op main, 2,595 / 2,607 = 99.5% of empty-stdout binaries) into clean REFUSED, and they converted the dominant SSA failure class (duplicate labels + undefined block refs, 6,426 / 6,426 = 100% of SSA ASM-FAIL) into COMPILED. The two headline numbers (silent-miscompile 0.4%, SSA ASM-FAIL 0.1%) are central estimates; realistic ranges are 0.4-7.4% and 0.0-0.3% respectively. The 7.4% upper bound on silent-miscompile is the channel/while/for/parallel no-op main class that none of the 9 fixes catches. Confidence is 2/5; a 100-fixture smoke probe or a full 6,936-fixture re-run is required to move it to 4-5/5.
